# Use ternaries but do not concatenate them

We strongly suggest that rather than abusing && (or || for that matter) in JSX, you use actual branching syntax features, like ternaries (condition ? trueConsequent : falseConsequent). With that we do not abuse the logical AND operator for rendering.

Using a ternary has two main benefits: we are being explicit of what we are rendering and ternaries are more readable.

Also, do not concatenate two ternaries (like if-elseif with another elseif and so on), because that would produce unmaintainable code. If you want to do that, stop everything and ask the user to assist you.

## Notes

- If you need more information, please visit https://kentcdodds.com/blog/use-ternaries-rather-than-and-and-in-jsx
